# Walkthrough — Unified Scraper Integration

We have integrated all three scraper implementations (local standard, local stealth, and cloud Browserbase) into a single, cohesive, smart-routing module at [scraper.py](file:///c:/Users/yasha/Desktop/scout/engine/scraper.py).

## Changes Made

### 1. Unified Scraper Interface
*   **Smart-Routing Fallback Chain:** The `fetch_page` function now accepts `method="auto"`. It attempts local `"stealth"` scraping first. If a bot check/block screen (like Cloudflare, Captcha, or Access Denied) is detected, it automatically falls back to `"browserbase"` (cloud CDP session) if `BROWSERBASE_API_KEY` is present. Otherwise, it falls back to local `"standard"` Playwright.
*   **Local Browser Context Sharing:** Standard and Stealth scrapers now share a single background Chromium process/event loop, significantly saving system memory and CPU overhead.
*   **Media Configuration:** Introduced `block_media=True/False` so callers can toggle media resource blocking (helpful if visual image assets are needed).
*   **Popup & Scroll Optimization:** Cleaned up and combined pop-up dismissals and scroll helpers into consolidated local routines.

### 2. Import Cleanup
*   Updated imports in [deep_extractor.py](file:///c:/Users/yasha/Desktop/scout/engine/deep_extractor.py) to reference [scraper.py](file:///c:/Users/yasha/Desktop/scout/engine/scraper.py).
*   Deleted the obsolete and redundant files: `scraper_stealth.py` and `scraper_browserbase.py`.

